; Pasture3D Water — Pond preset. Spec §6.
;
; The cheapest variant, and the versatility payoff: a pond is genuinely less work
; for the GPU, not the same shader tinted differently. Two waves, one detail
; layer, no scattering, no crest foam, no shadow receive — all compiled out.
;
; Drop it on any MeshInstance3D. No plugin, no Pasture3D node, no wiring (G6).
;
; Table generated by bench/WavePresetTables.gd from count 2, direction 55°,
; spread 50°, amplitude 0.05 m, max wavelength 12 m. Amplitude sum 0.076 m.
;
; Its shortest wave is 6.04 m, BELOW the 10 m figure in WaterWaves::MIN_WAVELENGTH,
; and that is deliberate rather than an escape. The floor is a float-precision
; limit at clipmap-scale coordinates (spec §3.1); a pond sits near its own origin
; and is not in that regime, so it gets ripples instead of two copies of one wave.
; A pond placed kilometres from the world origin IS back in that regime — set
; _water_domain_origin to the mesh's position if you put one there. It is an
; INSTANCE uniform, so that is MeshInstance3D.set_instance_shader_parameter(),
; not a value on this material; Pool3D does it for you from the node's position.
[gd_resource type="ShaderMaterial" load_steps=4 format=3]

